00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:02,000
The Swap is a comedy, tv movie film directed by Jay Karas.

2
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Based on the book by Megan Shull, The Swap follows the adventures of a rhythmic gymnast named Ellie with a make-it-or-break-it
competition, and the younger brother named Jack in a hockey family who's vying for a varsity spot on his school team.

3
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:54,000
But when a simple text causes the two to swap bodies,
their paths take an unexpected cross.

4
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Ellie O'Brien, played by Peyton List.

5
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Jack Malloy, played by Jacob Bertrand.

6
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Coach Malloy, played by Darrin Rose.

7
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:38,000
Summer, played by Claire Rankin.

8
00:47:28,000 --> 00:47:34,000
Gunner, played by Callan Potter.

9
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:30,000
Stryker, played by Jesse Bostick.

10
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:26,000
The Swap is a 2016 American television teen film that premiered on Disney Channel as
a part of the network's annual "Monstober" event on October 7, 2016.

11
01:05:16,000 --> 01:05:22,000
The film is based on the young adult novel of the same name written by Megan Shull and is
written by Charlie Shahnaian and Shari Simpson and directed by Jay Karas.

12
01:11:12,000 --> 01:11:18,000
The movie stars Peyton List and Jacob Bertrand.

13
01:17:08,000 --> 01:17:14,000
The film explores themes of high school, based on novel or
book, ice hockey, body-swap, rhythmic gymnastics.

14
01:23:04,000 --> 01:23:10,000
The tone is lighthearted.
